content.text:
I have enough evidence to conclude. The degradation traces to one fault: ts-preserve-service's outgoing calls to ts-seat-service are returned with status 401 even though seat-service answered 200, and preserve then fails its own requests with 500s that reach the UI.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-preserve-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_wrong_status_code",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.attr_http_response_status_code AS client_code, s.attr_http_response_status_code AS seat_server_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.trace_id = c.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id = c.span_id WHERE c.service_name = 'ts-preserve-service' AND c.attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND s.service_name = 'ts-seat-service' AND s.attr_span_kind = 'Server' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Preserve's client spans to seat-service show 401 in 537 calls, while seat's server spans report 200."
        },
